    phone: "(260) 438-9216", phoneHref: "+12604389216", web: "https://stmarysfw.org/aim-services/",
    desc: "Nonprofit ministry of St. Mary Mother of God Catholic Church that puts donated cars in the hands of people in dire need of transportation: working donated vehicles are repaired to safety standards, then sold at fair-market 'private party' price with NO interest — AIM covers all licensing and registration, monthly payments are based on your ability to pay, and you insure the car yourself (Indiana minimum required). Serves people with limited means including people coming out of homelessness, in recovery, abuse survivors, people recently released from prison, and people with disabilities — currently partnering with Vincent Village, A Mother's Hope, and the YWCA Women's Shelter. Apply with an eligibility application; there is a waiting list, and AIM always needs donated cars. Contact Ken Yahne at (260) 438-9216.",
