    desc: "Indiana Adult Protective Services investigates abuse, neglect (including self-neglect), and exploitation of endangered adults 18+ who can't protect themselves. The Fort Wayne office (formerly 'Unit 3' at the Keystone Building, 1st Floor, 602 S Calhoun St) used to cover Allen County — the state has since moved to regional teams. To make a report, call the statewide APS hotline at 1-800-992-6978 (toll-free) or file a report online — if someone is in immediate danger, call 911. Indiana law requires reporting; good-faith reporters are immune from civil and criminal liability. per in.gov/fssa, APS field investigations are now managed by FIVE regional teams — the old county-based hub/unit structure ended July 2025, so the Keystone Building 'Unit 3' office (602 S Calhoun St, (260) 449-7989) is legacy — call before visiting. To make a report, call the statewide APS hotline at 1-800-992-6978 (toll-free) or file a report online via the FSSA Adult Protective Services page — if someone is in immediate danger, call 911. Indiana law requires reporting; good-faith reporters are immune from civil and criminal liability.",
