    web: "https://www.shepherdshouse.org/",
    desc: "FREE long-term live-in recovery for homeless veterans 18+ (men) dealing with substance abuse or mental health. 41 beds at the main house + 6 graduate beds at a second house on Spy Run Ave. Stay: 6 months minimum up to 2 years. Commercial kitchen — residents take turns cooking on a rotating schedule (home-style meals, ~50 people/day); pray together before meals. Daily recovery sessions + nightly recovery meetings + AA Mondays 7 PM in-house + individual counseling, CBT, life-skills and budgeting classes, case management, VA/HUD housing help, employment counseling. Shared rooms/shared bathrooms. Welcome kit, toiletries, bedding, clothing all provided — bring nothing but yourself. RULES: must stay sober (random drug tests, negative test for entry), curfew 8 PM first 30 days then 10 PM, mandatory dinner Mon-Thu + weekly house meetings + evening programming, daily chores, 2 weekend passes/month, no romantic relationships between residents.",
