    desc: "City of Fort Wayne's official winter emergency shelter for single women and families with children, Dec 1, 2025 – Mar 31, 2026 at the Salvation Army: temporary emergency housing, showers, and three meals a day, open 24 hours a day for the first time (Blue Jacket provides staffing; the Rescue Mission helps pay and train; Bowen Health and Parkview send staff on site). Salvation Army general line (260) 744-2311. Expanded overnight shelter also runs at the Rescue Mission, St. Joseph Missions Women's Shelter, and Just Neighbors. Region 3 Winter Contingency Plan 2025-2026 (secure.in.gov, updated 1.16.25) confirms dates, 24/7 operation, direct WCES line 260-452-6086, 3 meals/day, Bowen/Parkview on-site staff; city engage page still shows 2025-2026 plan as current. 2026 outcomes (WPTA Apr 2026): 4,055 safe shelter nights, avg 33/night (peak 54), all FW shelters at 107% capacity; the first-ever winter shelter for single women and families with children housed 248 people incl. 47 children. The 2026-2027 plan was still not published as of 2026-10-03 (per Oct 2026 news search: WPTA Apr 2026 reports the city is 'working with the nonprofits again right now to come up with a plan similar to last winter's efforts' and the new Homeless Resource Center won't open in time for this winter; Aug 2026 City-County Council committee discussed winter contingency bed expansion — last winter's overnight warming center ran 50 nights, AIC configurable for 60 beds for future winters; everyonehomefw.org plan page still shows the older plan text) — call 211 in November for this winter's details. the 2026-2027 plan is still unpublished (WPTA Oct 1, 2026: the city is 'working with the nonprofits again right now to come up with a plan similar to last winter's efforts'); Salvation Army is still operating at 2901 N Clinton St (Oct 2026 Christmas-assistance intake there).",
